olor": "#232", "widgets_values": ["The user's raw input prompt is in Chinese: \"把图片比例改成3比4，不减少图片内容.\" which means \"Change the image ratio to 3:4, without reducing the image content.\"\n\nWait, but my task is to write a video generation prompt. The system prompt says I'm a creative assistant that expands user prompts into detailed video generation prompts. But the user's actual request here is just to change the aspect ratio to 3:4 without reducing content.\n\nHmm, this is an image editing task (aspect ratio change), not really a video generation task. But the output format requires a single concise paragraph in natural English, describing the transformation from the input image to the output.\n\nLet me think about what should happen. The input image is a wide banner (roughly 16:9, actually 1024x576 or so, looks like 16:9). It contains:\n- A deep blue/purple gradient background with glowing particle network effects on the right side and light streaks on the left.\n- Center text: \"全新图片编辑模型 Qwen2.1\" in large white bold characters.\n- Below it: \"支持 10 图编辑，文字准确无错字\" in smaller white text.\n- Bottom: a row of 10 small portrait images (rounded rectangles) showing various illustrations of women in traditional Chinese attire (hanfu), one landscape scene, etc.\n\nUser wants to change ratio to 3:4 (portrait) without reducing content. So the output should be a 3:4 portrait frame containing all elements: the 10 images in a row at the bottom, the title text centered, the background gradient and particle effects.\n\nSince the output must be 3:4 portrait, the layout needs to adapt: the row of 10 images will need to be rearranged to fit the narrower width — probably stacked in multiple rows, or the images scaled down. But the instruction says \"不减少图片内容\" (don't reduce image content), meaning all 10 images and the text must remain visible.\n\nMy job: generate a prompt guiding the transformation. Since this is essentially an aspect ratio change with content preservation, the prompt should describe: keep all elements (the 10 portrait thumbnails, the two lines of text, the background), rearrange them to fit a 3:4 portrait frame, e.g., arrange the 10 thumbnails in two rows of five (or three rows), keep the title text centered in the upper area, keep the deep blue gradient background with glowing network particles and light streaks.\n\nBut wait — the system prompt is for video generation. The output should be a video generation prompt. But the user's request is static image editing. The system says \"Given an image (first frame) and user Raw Input Prompt, generate a prompt to guide video generation from that image.\" Hmm, but the user's prompt doesn't ask for video. Still, I have to follow the output format: single concise paragraph in natural English, starting with Style if needed.\n\nActually, given the meta-task, maybe I should treat this as: the output is a 3:4 version of the same graphic. The \"video\" aspect is trivial — no motion requested. So the prompt should describe preserving everything while adapting the layout to 3:4.\n\nLet me carefully compose the prompt following the rules:\n- No forbidden expressions (\"such as\", \"etc.\", \"or\", \"approximately\", etc.).\n- Single paragraph, natural English.\n- Describe the transformation: extend/rearrange to 3:4 portrait.\n- Preserve all content: the 10 rounded rectangular thumbnails in a horizontal row at the bottom (in 3:4, arrange in two rows of five to keep all visible), the main title \"全新图片编辑模型 Qwen2.1\" centered, the subtitle \"支持 10 图编辑，文字准确无错字\" below it, the deep navy-to-purple gradient background with the constellation-like glowing node network on the right and purple light streaks on the left.\n\nWait, but the rule says don't re-describe established visual details? That rule is for video generation where the input image carries the details. Here the entire canvas is being rearranged; the layout change requires describing how elements are placed. Actually the rule \"Don't re-describe the input's existing content\" is about not causing drift. But for aspect ratio change, we need to specify the new layout. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what's most appropriate: the user wants the same content in 3:4. The safest prompt: \"Recompose the input graphic into a 3:4 portrait frame while keeping every element visible and unchanged in appearance: keep the horizontal row of ten rounded-corner thumbnail images along the bottom, rearranging them into two rows of five so all ten remain fully visible; keep the large white bold title"], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "anything", "link": 778, "label": "输入任何", "type": "*", "localized_name": "anything"}], "flags": {}, "type": "easy showAnything", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [492.11846923828125, 439.6435241699219], "pos": [514.5571899414062, 3273.429931640625], "id": 501, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfyui-easy-use", "ver": "d9c2072a2de5f51ef9898ec50ccd4dda82e16126", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.5.2"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "easy showAnything", "ttNbgOverride": {"bgcolor": "#335", "groupcolor": "#88A", "color": "#223"}}, "order": 21}, {"outputs": [{"name": "LATENT", "links": [735], "label": "Latent", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "Latent"}], "color": "#223", "widgets_values": [1024, 1024, 1], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "width"}, "name": "width", "link": 741, "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "宽度"}, {"widget": {"name": "height"}, "name": "height", "link": 742, "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "高度"}, {"widget": {"name": "batch_size"}, "name": "batch_size", "label": "batch_size", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "批次大小"}], "flags": {}, "type": "EmptyLatentImage", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#335", "size": [300, 120], "pos": [124.49404907226562, 2965.436279296875], "id": 480, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.36.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "inp